<title>GERMANY: German feeds industry welcomes EU gene-maize rule.</title>
<headline>German feeds industry welcomes EU gene-maize rule.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>German feeds industry association FFMI welcomed the European Commission decision to approve imports of genetically altered maize from the U.S., FFMI managing director Hubert Grote said.</p>
<p>&quot;It's a positive decision,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>National and EU laws did not provide for labelling of feed products derived from genetically modified maize if they were identical to conventional products, he added.</p>
<p>-Vera Eckert, Hamburg newsroom +49-40-41903275</p>
</text>
